@startuml agent_delegation_cli_flow
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/cli/CampusClawCommand.java, createAgentSession and configureDelegation.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java, configureRuntimeTools and handleDelegationToolCall.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/LocalAgentDispatcher.java, dispatch.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/TransientAgentRunner.java, run.
' Observed behavior: origin/main wired delegation through legacy ServerMode and SessionPool.
' Architecture change: the merged design wires delegation only for explicit managed CLI sessions; HTTP V1 remains independent.
title Managed CLI Agent Delegation Flow

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor User
participant CampusClawCommand as CLI
participant AgentRuntimeManager as RuntimeManager
participant AgentSession as ParentSession
participant AgentBindingResolver as Resolver
participant LocalAgentDispatcher as Dispatcher
participant TransientAgentRunner as Runner
participant AgentSession as ChildSession

User -> CLI: cli --agent-id parent
CLI -> RuntimeManager: prepare(parent)
RuntimeManager --> CLI: PreparedAgentRuntime
CLI -> ParentSession: setAgentRuntime(parent)
CLI -> ParentSession: setDelegationState(entry)
CLI -> ParentSession: initialize(config)

ParentSession -> Resolver: resolve(parent bindings, principal, chain)
Resolver --> ParentSession: effective child candidates
note right of ParentSession
invoke_agent is visible only when
at least one candidate is allowed
end note

User -> ParentSession: task
ParentSession -> Dispatcher: dispatch(target, child task, fallback model)
Dispatcher -> Resolver: validate(target at execution time)
Resolver --> Dispatcher: Allowed or Rejected

alt Allowed
  Dispatcher -> RuntimeManager: prepare(target)
  RuntimeManager --> Dispatcher: child runtime
  Dispatcher -> Runner: run(child runtime, child state, task)
  Runner -> ChildSession: create and initialize transient session
  Runner -> ChildSession: prompt(task)
  ChildSession --> Runner: final assistant answer
  Runner --> Dispatcher: answer text
  Dispatcher --> ParentSession: override tool result
else Rejected or failed
  Dispatcher --> ParentSession: error tool result
end

note over CLI,ParentSession
Plain CLI sessions do not receive DelegationState.
HTTP V1 reads the shared .campusclaw location without entering this materialization flow.
end note
@enduml
